  "body": "﻿Process change: yes\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\nMove toolpath start and exit picks from links.approach to operation-level PathPicks across OpParams.\n\n- **Operation-level storage:** Store picks: PathPicks directly on each operation parameter variant (OpParams::*). PathPicks holds start: Vec<PathPick> and exit: Vec<PathPick>.\n- **Project format migration:** Load legacy .camproj files with start_point and exit_point under links.approach, or legacy WireContour with start coordinates, and migrate them to the operation-level picks field.\n- **Digest and caching:** Stamp operation picks in OpParams::stamp_picks with distinct markers (xC7 for start, xC8 for exit), preserving legacy digests when picks are empty. Contour operations with start or exit picks write pick bytes after links, which changes their digest; they must be generated again one time after an update.\n- **MCP and script surface:** Expose picks with start and exit points in MCP operation edit and add commands, validating against pick capabilities per operation type. Accept legacy keys (start on wire contour, start_point and exit_point under links.approach) on the MCP and script patch path and migrate them into picks.\n- **Decision document:** Added docs/decisions/3339-operation-level-picks.md.\n\n### Readings and Verification\n\n- cargo clippy -j 4 -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings: passed (0 warnings).\n- Pinning tests passed:\n  - contour_start_point (10/10)\n  - start_exit_shared (4/4)\n  - wire_stamp (7/7)\n  - mcp_wire_contour (8/8)\n  - wire_contour (8/8)\n  - mcp_edit_machine (8/8)\n  - ^Ggie_native (33/33)\n  - cut_recipe (20/20)\n  - sketch_engrave_trace (12/12)\n  - camcraft-ui (\native_post_dialog_*, 3/3)\n\n### What Was Not Exercised\n\n- Multi-point pick chains (single pick per role supported in this stage).\n\nChangelog: Toolpath start and exit points now store as operation-level picks across all operation types. Operations with start or exit picks must be generated again one time after an update.\n\nFixes #3339\r\n",
